## What can and cannot be concluded

- **Observed:** queued jump effects differ at3001 under rendering/movie/screenshot context. Same-source headless succeeds from the exact same prefix. It is a real observer/runtime-context robustness failure, not proof that the whole geometric route is impossible.
- **TTL:** Router has a0.1-second wall-clock age filter, and nearby live `get_image()/save_png` can plausibly delay consumption. But this old trace strips queue timestamp/epoch from its exported input snapshots and does not record consume age or silent expiry/drop cause. Therefore no direct evidence proves TTL expiry. Per-frame controller increments do not measure wall time.
- **Driver/geometry:** inherited driver emits the intended jump and all source/geometry/prefix facts agree. Timing sensitivity remains possible; exact attribution among input expiry, runtime action eligibility and rendering/observer scheduling is not established. Do not modify Motor, RouterTTL or driver to force this artifact to pass.

Bounded evidence saved in `outer_render_failure_review.json`, `.window.json`, `.provenance.json`, `.log`, with actual independently run `.py` exit0. This review reads two Scene captures and small source/receipt/log/PNG evidence only; no engine, browser, FFmpeg or large cohort recomputation.

## Failure packaging and one proposed diagnostic control

Archiving/encoding the existing failed AVI into a complete failed MP4 is legitimate evidence retention. A derived receipt must remain `failed_route_media_preserved`, record original process exit1/7assertions/1failure and3007tick failed outcome, preserve original raw/log/receipt/AVI hashes, and distinguish encoding-time source equality from the original producer's absent source_after. Accepting failed members into a packager is **not** lowering the original execution gate. It must not change the old native receipt/queue, claim a completed cycle, or turn the media-conversion exit0 into gameplay PASS. Future parent metadata must include this failure alongside the9 prior unresolved policy cases.

A single serial diagnostic run without live PNG reads may keep route-check equivalence if it still calls the same inherited run_case/custom_route/SceneTrace.tick/observe at the same sampling frequency, retains actual route_target, complete cycle_return, issue checks and Manifest invariance, and only disables `capture_screen` readback/PNG writes. Do not remove observe/finish early or replace the route. Its producer is a distinct **no-live-PNG diagnostic control**: it must explicitly not satisfy the old screenshot-nonempty observation contract. Full movie frames may be extracted afterward and labelled video_frame/time rather than exact physics ticks. Even success would support an association with live screenshot observation, not establish TTL as the cause or erase the first failed attempt. Waiting for the currently active observation closure to finish before at most one such run avoids concurrent-engine confounding. This reviewer has not executed that proposed control or accepted its result.
